  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Arizona total $236M for FY2027 to date. The state recorded 1,121 awards with an average award size of $211K. Obligations are down 99.3% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows obligations of $16.4B in FY22, $20.9B in FY23, $19.3B in FY24, $25.6B in FY25, $34.7B in FY26, and $236M in FY27. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buying agency in FY2027 to date with $96.1M, followed by the Department of the Treasury with $67.5M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $17.4M. FCN, INC. is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $67.3M, followed by JACOBS ENGINEERING GROUP INC. with $13.7M and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. with $13.5M. Other Computer Related Services leads industries with $69.9M, followed by Engineering Services with $14.2M and All Other Business Support Services with $13.7M.",
